<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#tisha-bav">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tisha B'Av</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tisha B'Av, the ninth day of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> month of Av, is the annual fast day in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaism">Judaism</a> that mourns the destruction of the First Temple by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonians">Babylonians</a> in 587 or 586 BCE and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-in-jerusalem">Second Temple</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in 70 CE. Other disasters of Jewish history are also remembered on it, and the Book of Lamentations is read in synagogues.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tisha-bav.jpg" alt="Tisha B'Av" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Didier Descouens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:(Venice)_La_distruzione_del_tempio_di_Gerusalemme_-Francesco_Hayez_-_gallerie_Accademia_Venice.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The idea that a dynasty of David would be restored became the root of messianic expectation, and the destruction of the First Temple, commemorated on <b>Tisha B’Av</b>, remains a defining memory in Jewish tradition.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-judah">Kingdom of Judah · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>It is recited before the Grace After Meals on weekdays (Psalm 126 replaces it on the Sabbath, holidays and festive meals) and before <b>Tisha B'Av</b>, the fast that mourns the destruction of the Temples in Jerusalem.</blockquote><a href="/songs/psalm-137">Psalm 137</a></li><li><blockquote>The day, <b>Tisha B'Av</b> in the Hebrew calendar, fell on either 4 or 30 August.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-30">30 August in history</a></li></ul></section>
